## Workflow
- New feature or unclear requirement → `spec` skill → `architect` skill → build. Skip both when
  the change fits in one sentence.
- Every spec ends with a runnable verify step. Run it before calling work done.
- Recurring task (~3×) or a repeated mistake → `tailor` can generate a project skill.

## Memory rule
- After a decision or insight: `wiki` skill, op `record`. Supersede, never delete. One fact lives
  in one place; everything else links to it.
- Before ending a session that changed things: `wiki` skill, op `status`.

## Guardrails
- Hooks in `.claude/hooks/` classify every rule by domain and class (P0 lock … P4 audit); see
  `.claude/hooks/README.md`. Guard files (`.claude/hooks/**`, `.claude/settings*.json`,
  `.pre-commit-config.yaml`) are locked for Claude: ask the user to change them.
- Never paste or copy secret values; refer to env var names.
- If a hook blocks something that looks wrong, tell the user. Do not work around it.

